{
  "format": "sfxgen/1",
  "name": "Motorbike rev",
  "description": "A rider on a parallel-twin motorbike at a red light, blipping the throttle. At idle the twin beats steadily, each firing a little different, with the valve gear clattering lightly on top: a dense, dark, rumbling body, the silencer's chambers smearing each firing into the next. A first short blip, throttle shut, back down; then a longer, harder one, higher, that hangs for a moment, the intake roaring and the open pipes ripping. When the throttle snaps shut the fuel is cut: the firings go weak and hollow, unburnt fuel pops and crackles in the hot pipes as the revs fall, and the engine settles back to its idle. Loud aftermarket pipes, a street with buildings on both sides.",
